                                                The following update was added:<br/>
                                                <br/>On August 27, Amadeus monitoring tools detected increased latency in shopping transactions, followed by customer reports of errors and response timeouts across various Amadeus applications. This impacted users' ability to complete or manage passenger bookings.<br/>

<br/>Investigations revealed issue with a Couchbase cluster linked to the shopping environment, affecting both Master Pricer and Flex Pricer. As part of the recovery process, Amadeus support teams rerouted traffic away from the impacted server, redistributed it across other data center regions, scaled up server resources, and recycled application processes to stabilize performance. These actions led to the initial recovery of Flex Pricer at 07:50 GMT. The same recovery steps were applied to Master Pricer, with traffic gradually reintroduced to prevent load spikes and ensure stability. Positive results were observed, confirming recovery for Master Pricer. The incident was fully recovered at 15:38 GMT. &nbsp;All environments remain under heightened monitoring to ensure continued stability.<br/>
